## GitHub Issues

All 5 distinct problems have been filed as separate issues in the public triage repo:

- [Issue #1: Wrong Day of Week on Invite](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/1) — 111 reports
- [Issue #4: Appointment Auto-Moved Without User Action](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/4) — 34 reports
- [Issue #5: Reminder Sent on Wrong Date](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/5) — 37 reports
- [Issue #6: Other Date/Time Issues (Triage Required)](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/6) — 113 reports
- [Issue #7: Date Format Parsing Error (DD/MM vs MM/DD)](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/7) — 132 reports

(Issues #2 and #3 were merged into #7)

## Lessons

- A merged ticket that looks like one issue often contains multiple independent bugs.
- Overlapping categories signal a root cause that spans multiple surface symptoms. When two categories describe the same underlying failure, merge them.
- Locale-aware date handling requires consistent application across all systems (booking, invite, reminder, display).
- A 26% "other" category is a signal to continue triage, not a reason to stop.
- Categorization requires reading individual reports, not just subject lines.

